    "label": {
      "en": "Energy credit First Announced in B23. First Payment in 2022."
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$benergy_amt"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "This constant sets the per-account (tax unit) amount of Ireland's Electricity/Energy Credit, a one-off, universal, non-means-tested lump-sum credit deducted directly from domestic electricity bills, paid to all domestic energy account holders who are not on a low-usage account. It is used in the benergy_cred_ie policy's BenCalc function as the Comp_perTU parameter, i.e. the credit is computed and awarded once per tax unit (household energy account) rather than per person. The latest value is €125, consistent with the one-off €125 instalment paid in January 2025 described in the Country Report and benefits documentation; earlier years saw larger total support (e.g. €250 paid in two €125 instalments across late 2024/early 2025) reflecting the temporary cost-of-living measures introduced from Budget 2023 (first announced/paid in 2022), which the sources note were discontinued from 2026. The credit is exempt from tax and social insurance contributions and is fully simulated in EUROMOD."
    },
